[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113329,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 67,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Oncocytoma is a benign encapsulated neoplasm composed of large epithelial cells with abundant eosinophilic granular cytoplasm due to the accumulation of mitochondria.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:09:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113330,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 67,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8290/0 Oncocytoma</p>\r\n<p>8290/0 Clear cell oncocytoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:09:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113331,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 67,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E91.1 &amp; XH9Z86 Benign neoplasm of other specified major salivary glands &amp; Oxyphilic adenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:09:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113332,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 67,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> oncocytic adenoma, oxyphilic adenoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:09:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113333,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 67,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Clear cell oncocytoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:09:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113334,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 67,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>More than 80% of cases occur in the parotid, approximately 10% occur in the submandibular gland, and the rest occur in minor salivary glands and the sublingual gland {2031528; 2361662; 8940996; 12087334}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:09:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113335,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 67,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Symptoms depend on anatomical location. Oncocytoma usually presents as a unilateral painless swelling.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:09:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113336,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 67,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Oncocytomas represent &lt;&nbsp;1.5% of salivary gland tumours. The incidence peak is in the seventh decade of life, with no sex predilection {2031528; 2361662}. Tumours may be multifocal and bilateral {2917323; 18357950; 22627459}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:09:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113337,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 67,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A history of radiotherapy or long-term radiation exposure has been reported {2031528}. The oncocytic phenotype is associated with mitochondrial DNA mutations {12087334; 20732299}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:09:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113338,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 67,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Oncocytoma may arise in the background of multinodular oncocytic hyperplasia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:09:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113339,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 67,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Oncocytomas are usually small, single, lobulated, well-circumscribed, brownish tumours with or without a cystic component and/or central fibrosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:09:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113340,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 67,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Oncocytomas are well-circumscribed tumours consisting of oncocytes with abundant eosinophilic granular cytoplasm, arranged in nests and sheets, separated by a thin fibrovascular stroma. The nuclei are uniform, vesicular, and centrally placed, with prominent single nucleoli. Dark cells with pyknotic nuclei, probably representing degenerated oncocytes, are present. Tumours lack entrapped normal parenchyma.</p>\r\n<h5>Subtype</h5>\r\n<p>In clear cell oncocytoma, the presence of glycogen and fixation artefacts causes the clear cell change {3402976}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry and differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The presence of p63-positive basal cells excludes metastatic renal cell carcinoma and acinic cell carcinoma {20614263; 19646823}. An absence of PAX2 and/or PAX8 expression favours oncocytoma over metastatic renal carcinoma {24771139}. <em>MAML2</em> rearrangement helps distinguish oncocytic mucoepidermoid carcinoma {33002921}. SOX10 and S100 immunopositivity and <em>PLAG1</em> gene rearrangement distinguishes pleomorphic adenoma and myoepithelioma with extensive oncocytic metaplasia {32673681}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:09:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113341,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 67,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Smears of oncocytoma are indistinguishable from those of nodular oncocytic hyperplasia {31051720}. The nuclei tend to be round, with prominent nucleoli. Acinic cell carcinoma can be distinguished by the finely vacuolated cytoplasm that is often lost in smears. A DOG1, p63, and S100 panel on FNA cell blocks is useful in differential diagnosis {31051720}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:09:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 588,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113342,
        "bookId": 52,
